{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Knives(?)</b> — basins to receive the blood of the offerings." "<b>Of a second kind</b> — golden basins." "<b>And ten other vessels</b> — which are not mentioned by name, a thousand; and he mentioned their particulars, which are included in them: two thousand four hundred and ninety-nine. And in my opinion: so too the particulars, which are two thousand three hundred ninety-nine in their entirety, are the large vessels, and afterward he included them among large and small, which are five thousand four hundred; and so it is written in Chronicles: \"and all the vessels of the house of Elohim, the great and the small, and the treasures of the king's house, all he brought to Babylon.\""], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:41:33.708121668Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}